4. Create a function genderIsoCalc.m that returns four outputs.
  maleIsoIndMeans: Days 1,2,3 averages for men
  femaleIsoIndMeans: Days 1,2,3 averages for women
  maleGroupIsoMean: Average of Days 1,2,3 for men
  femaleGroupIsoMean: Average of Days 1,2,3 for women
  %CREATE GENDER FUNCTION
  %This function operates to help you find the average of male and female
  %performance for each day and as a cumulative averages of days 1-3. Days 1,
  %2, and 3 denoted as d1, d2, and d3, respectively.
    function [maleIsoIndMeans,maleGroupIsoMean,femaleIsoIndMeans, femaleGroupIsoMean] = genderIsoCalc(gender,d1,d2,d3)
       for i=1:length(gender)
          if gender(i) == 'M'
              d1m = mean(d1);
              d2m = mean(d2);
              d3m = mean(d3);
          elseif gender(i) == 'F'
                d1f = mean(d1);
                d2f = mean(d2);
                d3f = mean(d3);
         end
      end
              maleIsoIndMeans = [d1m,d2m,d3m]
              maleGroupIsoMean = mean(maleIsoIndMeans)
              femaleIsoIndMeans = [d1f,d2f,d3f]
              femaleGroupIsoMean = mean(femaleIsoIndMeans)
    end
  
  %EXECUTE GENDER FUNCTION
  [subID, age, gender, weight, d1, d2, d3] = importfile('isok_data_6803.csv');
  [maleIsoIndMeans,maleGroupIsoMean,femaleIsoIndMeans, femaleGroupIsoMean] = genderIsoCalc(gender,d1,d2,d3)
  

5. Create a function dayComparer.m for Days 1-2 and 2-3.
  %CREATE DAY FUNCTION
  %The purpose of this function it to call every subject that improved either
  %from Day 1 to Day 2, or from Day 2 to Day 3.
  function [day1toDay2,day2toDay3] = dayComparer(subID,d1,d2,d3)
      day1toDay2 = [];
      day2toDay3 = [];
  for i = 1:length(subID)
          if d2(i)>d1(i)
              day1toDay2 = [day1toDay2; subID(i)];
        end
      if d3(i)>d2(i)
               day2toDay3 = [day2toDay3; subID(i)];
         end
     end
   end
  
  %EXECUTE DAY FUNCTION
  [day1toDay2,day2toDay3] = dayComparer(subID,d1,d2,d3)
  

6. Weight normalize the data and calculate group means for each day. These should be stored as normDay1mean, normDay2mean, and normDay3mean.
  %CREATE NORM FUNCTION
  %This function normalizes the weight across the 3 days.
  %normdn normalizes each subject for the nth day.
  %normDaynmean is the average of all participants (now with normalized
  %weight) across the 3 days.
    function [normDay1mean,normDay2mean,normDay3mean] = daysweightnorm(weight,d1,d2,d3)
    for i = 1:length(weight)
    normd1 = d1(i)./weight(i)
    normd2 = d2(i)./weight(i)
    normd3 = d3(i)./weight(i)
    normDay1mean = mean(normd1)
    normDay2mean = mean(normd2)
    normDay3mean = mean(normd3)
    end
  %EXECUTE NORM FUNCTION
  [normDay1mean,normDay2mean,normDay3mean] = daysweightnorm(weight,d1,d2,d3)

